DESCRIPTION >
    Wave-3 flexible_report Class-A dim-swap: group_by=CONVERSION_TYPE (FINAL Class-A sibling). Clone of
    flexible_report_stitching_method_by_site with the dim expr swapped to GROUP_COLUMNS.conversion_type
    and the SAME external_event_id dedup carried from birth (#170). One row per conversion_type.

    DIFFERENT SHAPE (verified — NOT the multiIf mould of provider/attribution_status/stitching_method):
    GROUP_COLUMNS.conversion_type is an INLINE expr (not a named _SQL const) and is a PLAIN column read
    with a STATIC fallback: COALESCE(NULLIF(properties.conversion_type, ''), 'untyped') — an empty/absent
    conversion_type buckets as 'untyped'. NO multiIf, NO ingestion_method/stitching_method reference.
    Still Class-A: model-independent (same expr for all 4 touch models + ai_platforms), references ONLY
    the conversion event's own conversion_type, NO _nd touchpoint columns. So the window is a no-op (same
    reasoning as the siblings, proven GREEN on --live) and this ONE pipe serves group_by=conversion_type
    for all 4 touch models.

    dim = the conversion_type dim expr, typed-translated (§2.6): properties.conversion_type ->
    conversion_type (LowCardinality(Nullable(String)), events.datasource:31). EMPTY/NULL convention
    replicated EXACTLY (its own: static 'untyped', NOT a multiIf): COALESCE(NULLIF(conversion_type,''),
    'untyped'). metric in {revenue, conversions} via the `metric` param. BASE-CASE GATE ONLY (no
    dim2/custom/filters, UTC, conversion_date); window-tolerant. NOTE: group_by=conversion_type (the
    DIM) is distinct from filter_conversion_type (a content filter) — a filtered request is gated to
    HogQL (filterClauses!==''), so this pipe never sees one. Same params/output columns (dim_value,
    metric_value) so the wiring's positional remap stays byte-identical.

    external_event_id DEDUP (identical to the sibling pipes, #170): keep all null/empty-keyed rows; for a
    non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered, matching
    HogQL). Tie-break Tinybird event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate (it
    shares conversion_type+value). PARAM SHAPE: {{ String(site_id) }} referenced TWICE (outer + dedup
    subquery); date params once. MANDATORY before deploy: `tb --cloud deploy --check` (ST_Staging, NOT
    prod). VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN.

NODE flexible_report_conversion_type_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(NULLIF(conversion_type, ''), 'untyped') AS dim_value,
        {% if String(metric, 'conversions') == 'revenue' %}
        SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)))
        {% else %}
        countIf(lower(coalesce(conversion_type, '')) != 'refund')
        {% end %} AS metric_value
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
      -- external_event_id dedup — carried from the sibling pipes (#170), faithful port of the HogQL
      -- leg (attribution-engine.js:2397-2409). KEEP every null/empty-keyed row; for a non-null key
      -- keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered). Tie-break Tinybird
      -- event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate.
      AND (
        external_event_id IS NULL
        OR external_event_id = ''
        OR event_id IN (
          SELECT argMin(event_id, timestamp)
          FROM events
          WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
            AND event_type = '$conversion'
            AND external_event_id IS NOT NULL
            AND external_event_id != ''
          GROUP BY external_event_id
        )
      )
    GROUP BY dim_value
    ORDER BY metric_value DESC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
